      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "626c2da0",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "1. Analytical Contribution\n",
                "\n",
                "A short section clearly stating how this study extends traditional response-time evaluation by:\n",
                "\n",
                "- Emphasizing tail-risk metrics rather than averages\n",
                "- Integrating survival analysis with statistical testing\n",
                "- Combining predictive modeling with explainable AI\n",
                "- Enabling structured cross-city comparison\n",
                "\n",
                "This section should explicitly differentiate the methodology from conventional descriptive approaches.\n",
                "\n",
                "2. Structural Performance Differences\n",
                "\n",
                "Combine:\n",
                "\n",
                "- Cross-City Performance Summary\n",
                "- Log-rank statistical support\n",
                "- Central vs tail differences\n",
                "\n",
                "Everything about “which city performs differently” lives here\n",
                "\n",
                "3. When & Where Risk Concentrates\n",
                "\n",
                "Combine:\n",
                "\n",
                "- Temporal Risk Insights\n",
                "- Spatial & Operational Insights\n",
                "- Time + location are both structural context.<br>They belong together. \n",
                "\n",
                "4. Delay Drivers & System Interpretation\n",
                "\n",
                "Combine:\n",
                "\n",
                "- Model-based delay drivers\n",
                "- SHAP insights\n",
                "- Operational interpretation\n",
                "\n",
                "Put drivers + meaning together.This avoids separating “drivers” and “implications” artificially."
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
